# Jarvis Central Dashboard

Website: {{SITE_URL}} (password + authenticator; the owner's only).
Tool repo: `{{REPO}}` — `app/` website, `agent/` scripts, `docs/architecture.md` API contract, `CLAUDE.md` rules for changing the tool.
Projects: every folder under `{{PROJECTS_ROOT}}` is a project (id = folder name, slugified) with a `CLAUDE.md` and a `PRD.md`.
**The website is the single source of truth for checklists.**

## The CLI (use this, not raw HTTP)
`node {{REPO}}/agent/jarvis.mjs <command>` — reads `~/.config/jarvis/env` (URL + agent token). `help` lists everything:
- `projects` · `items <project> [--open] [--section S]` · `item <project> <id>`
- `set <project> <id> status=done due=YYYY-MM-DD note="…"` · `add <project> <section> "title" --due D --owner claude`
- `inbox [--project P]` · `reply <message-id> "text" --status answered|done|needs_you`
- `todo add "title" --date today --project P --item ID` · `todos`
- `reviews --project P --type project|recap|coaching|jarvis|doc|security --full`
- `audits <project>` — security audit reports mirrored from the project's audits folder (date, verdict, headline)
Owner values: `founder` = the owner (you'd say "you"), `claude`, `both`.

## At session start in a project folder
1. `jarvis inbox --project <id>`: mention waiting messages. The background worker normally answers within a minute;
   only pick one up if it's `new` and older than ~10 min (worker offline) — then `reply` when done.
2. `jarvis items <id> --open` for the live checklist when planning work. Items set to `doing` with owner `claude`
   are a go signal.

## During / end of session
- Finished something on the checklist → `jarvis set <project> <id> status=done`. New work discovered → `jarvis add`.
- Never mark an item done that isn't done. Due-date moves are logged and show up as "slipped" in Monday reviews.
- A new project → "Start new project" on the Admin page (or `node {{REPO}}/agent/setup.mjs new "<name>"`). A new folder → `projects.mjs sync`; the worker then runs the setup session (`setup.mjs queue <id>` runs it by hand).

## Changing Jarvis itself
Follow `{{REPO}}/CLAUDE.md`: personal changes go in `jarvis.config.json` (never committed); tool changes are generic,
go through a branch + PR, and get a CHANGELOG line.

## What runs by itself (`node {{REPO}}/agent/schedule.mjs show`)
- worker: inbox → `claude -p` in the project (code only on a `jarvis/<id>` branch + PR, never merges).
- planner: the week's plan → todos + Google/Apple calendars.
- weekly: per-project advisor reviews, recap, "working with AI" coaching, Jarvis usage review.
